      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That's double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A dose that high raises the risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nSome possible intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily with meals\n- **500 to 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals**, a more typical regimen\n\nTell me which dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If 1,700 mg three times daily is what you meant, please confirm that. I'd still suggest checking it with pharmacy first, and I'd add a note to the order documenting the rationale."
      }
